1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Everything we have learned so far is hanging here.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Shall we review them one by one?

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,042
Now, today is our last lesson. It is good to see you all. I am proud of every one of you for coming this far.

4
00:00:16,042 --> 00:00:20,025
Twenty-four weeks are over; today is the last lesson.

5
00:00:20,025 --> 00:00:23,482
'수료' [su-ryo] means you have finished the whole course.

6
00:00:26,212 --> 00:00:30,337
The final consonants '어려웠어요' [eo-ryeo-wo-sseo-yo] (were hard),

7
00:00:30,337 --> 00:00:36,072
but when the letters came together it '재미있었어요' [jae-mi-i-sseo-sseo-yo] (was fun).

8
00:00:36,522 --> 00:00:40,660
Today we look back over twenty-four weeks - the letters,

9
00:00:40,660 --> 00:00:43,690
the street words, the words of the heart.

10
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:44,872
'함께' [ham-kke] (together).

11
00:00:49,952 --> 00:00:56,312
You worked '열심히' [yeol-sim-hi] (hard) for twenty-four weeks - not one day was easy.

12
00:00:58,322 --> 00:01:04,512
Now close your eyes - twenty-four weeks go by '함께' [ham-kke] (together).

13
00:01:07,672 --> 00:01:09,428
The classroom fades,

14
00:01:09,428 --> 00:01:13,292
and everything we '배웠어요' [bae-wo-sseo-yo] (learned) rises up.

15
00:01:14,582 --> 00:01:17,033
An old fortress wall remains underground,

16
00:01:17,033 --> 00:01:19,125
and letters rise above it - heaven,

17
00:01:19,125 --> 00:01:20,082
earth and human.

18
00:01:22,782 --> 00:01:29,112
Consonants copy the shape of the mouth - 'ㄱ' [g] the root of the tongue,

19
00:01:29,112 --> 00:01:30,322
'ㅁ' [m] the lips.

20
00:01:31,372 --> 00:01:34,138
Trace them with me: 'ㅅ' [s], 'ㅈ' [j], 'ㅎ' [h].

21
00:01:34,138 --> 00:01:37,392
Strokes go top to bottom, left to right.

22
00:01:41,732 --> 00:01:45,792
Put a consonant and a vowel together and you get one block-like syllable.

23
00:01:47,722 --> 00:01:50,074
Count: 하나, 둘, 셋.

24
00:01:50,074 --> 00:01:56,102
Korean counts numbers two different ways.

25
00:01:57,842 --> 00:02:00,214
To ask the time: '몇 시예요?

26
00:02:00,214 --> 00:02:03,772
' [myeot si-ye-yo] (what time is it?

27
00:02:03,772 --> 00:02:08,022
) - 한 시 [han si], 두 시 [du si], 세 시 [se si].

28
00:02:08,992 --> 00:02:14,252
Down the corridor to the gallery - the letters we learned over twenty-four weeks hang on the walls.

29
00:02:16,182 --> 00:02:19,537
When you're curious at an exhibition, ask '이건 뭐예요?

30
00:02:19,537 --> 00:02:21,886
' [i-geon mwo-ye-yo] (what is this?

31
00:02:21,886 --> 00:02:23,362
) - it works anywhere.

32
00:02:25,132 --> 00:02:30,145
To talk about what you saw: '좋았어요' [jo-a-sseo-yo] (it was good),

33
00:02:30,145 --> 00:02:34,852
'멋있었어요' [meo-si-sseo-sseo-yo] (it was wonderful) - past-tense words.

34
00:02:35,422 --> 00:02:40,481
We also '배웠어요' [bae-wo-sseo-yo] (learned) the words you use outside - in shops,

35
00:02:40,481 --> 00:02:42,602
on the street, on the bus.

36
00:02:45,062 --> 00:02:46,920
In a shop you ask '얼마예요?

37
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:49,475
' [eol-ma-ye-yo] (how much is it?

38
00:02:49,475 --> 00:02:52,262
) - the shortest way to ask a price.

39
00:02:53,692 --> 00:02:59,312
If you want it cheaper: '깎아 주세요' [kka-kka ju-se-yo] - and it works better with a smile.

40
00:03:02,712 --> 00:03:05,187
On the street: '어떻게 가요?

41
00:03:05,187 --> 00:03:08,522
' - by subway, by bus, on foot.

42
00:03:13,462 --> 00:03:15,647
To give directions: go left, go right,

43
00:03:15,647 --> 00:03:16,682
go straight ahead.

44
00:03:24,212 --> 00:03:30,672
When you ask about hobbies you also ask how often - '자주' [ja-ju] (often) is an adverb.

45
00:03:31,912 --> 00:03:38,492
We also '배웠어요' [bae-wo-sseo-yo] (learned) how to speak the heart - the slow kind of talk.

46
00:03:38,942 --> 00:03:41,534
Describe your day: get up, eat, work, sleep.

47
00:03:41,534 --> 00:03:42,712
In order, it's easy.

48
00:03:50,962 --> 00:03:54,132
For weather: it's clear, it's raining, it's windy.

49
00:03:58,852 --> 00:04:02,166
You can speak feelings too: glad, upset, excited.

50
00:04:02,166 --> 00:04:03,992
Saying it makes it lighter.

51
00:04:09,312 --> 00:04:10,963
To give an opinion,

52
00:04:10,963 --> 00:04:15,742
start with '제 생각에는' [je saeng-ga-ge-neun] (in my opinion) - gentle and clear.

53
00:04:18,502 --> 00:04:23,972
Last week: making an appointment and coordinating times - you need both to meet as a group.

54
00:04:30,492 --> 00:04:33,370
Open your eyes - back in the classroom.

55
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:36,322
'덕분에' [deok-ppu-ne] (thanks to) you, we came this far.

56
00:04:39,102 --> 00:04:43,219
We looked back over all twenty-four weeks.

57
00:04:43,219 --> 00:04:45,082
'잘했어요' [jal-hae-sseo-yo] (well done).

58
00:04:45,532 --> 00:04:47,200
Now I will call your names.

59
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,931
What do you want to do next?

60
00:04:48,931 --> 00:04:53,812
'하고 싶어요' [ha-go si-peo-yo] means 'I want to do' - use it for what you wish for.

61
00:04:57,482 --> 00:05:03,877
Come forward for the certificate - the giver says '축하합니다' [chu-ka-ham-ni-da],

62
00:05:03,877 --> 00:05:06,192
the receiver '고맙습니다' [go-map-sseum-ni-da].

63
00:05:08,352 --> 00:05:11,902
And a bouquet too - flowers for someone who walked twenty-four weeks.

64
00:05:14,322 --> 00:05:18,754
Now you can say it: '자신 있어요' [ja-sin i-sseo-yo] (I feel confident).

65
00:05:18,754 --> 00:05:21,062
Say it to each other too.

66
00:05:21,512 --> 00:05:24,110
Now everybody stand up.

67
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:29,983
Study does not end here - it goes on '앞으로' [a-peu-ro] (onward),

68
00:05:29,983 --> 00:05:32,242
'계속' [gye-sok] (continuously)!

69
00:05:35,274 --> 00:05:41,274
Now let's all go outside - everyone is waiting for us.

70
00:05:41,274 --> 00:05:50,274
Everyone has gathered in the plaza. This is not the end - it goes on, onward and continuously.

71
00:05:50,274 --> 00:06:40,274
♪

